+`unsupported_platform_action`, `action_failed`, `outcome_unknown`. The last
+code is used when private-topic creation raises or returns no id because Telegram
+may have accepted the write before the transport failed; callers must inspect native
+topic/config state and must not blindly retry. Actions validate that the
 target adapter exists and is connected before acting; a disconnected or
 missing adapter degrades to a structured error, never an exception.
 
+`send_card` uses compact namespaced actions. Telegram re-authorizes the real
+callback actor/chat/thread and publishes a normalized `plugin_callback` through
+the existing `gateway_platform_event` hook. A hook may return
+`{"plugin": "my-plugin", "card": {"text": "...", "buttons": [...]}}`;
+Telegram edits the same message. Because the handler is registered at plugin
+startup and the payload contains only stable action/entity identifiers,
+read-only navigation survives a Gateway restart without a UI-state database.
+Use separate expiring application confirmation tokens for mutations.
+`update_card` updates such a card by stable chat/message id without exposing
+the Telegram SDK object, which lets supervised plugin tasks publish completion.
+
+Plugins that implement bounded fast actions may register
+`post_auth_pre_agent_dispatch`. It runs for an authorized, non-command user
